A plain answer is not a tool turn. A chat message with no tool call is billed as an ordinary message (~1 CR), not as a tool turn
(~3 CR) — the terminal charges for what the turn actually did, not for which tab you were on. Roughly a thousand tokens per credit,
so a short question costs the one-credit minimum and a long one with a lot of context costs more.
The two voice meters are separate and can both run at once. Dictation bills the microphone; spoken replies bill the answer
being read aloud. Push-to-talk closes the mic after a single message; the Voice toggle holds it open until you switch it off — and the
minimum is one minute either way. Reading the same answer on screen is free.
177
[PAGE 177 END]
09 Trading and execution T R A D I N G  P R I C E S  ·  0 9
Placing orders is free — deliberately and permanently (§06). What is metered is the server doing work: running an engine,
sweeping parameters, reconciling against a broker.
Action Where Shape Price
Paper trade Paper trading → every fill Fixed, per fill 0.05 CR
Backtest run Algo Trading → Backtest Lab → RUN BACKTEST Fixed 1 CR
Optimiser sweep Algo Trading → Backtest Lab → OPTIMISE Fixed 5 CR
Server screener run Algo Trading → Scanner → SERVER SCAN Fixed 1 CR
Broker reconciliation Equity Trading → bottom panel → RECONCILE Fixed 1 CR
Algo runtime Algo Trading → deploy a strategy Recurring · ~60 CR a month 2 CR/day
The distinctions worth knowing
A local backtest is free. The 1 CR is for the server engine; a backtest that runs on your own machine is not labelled
with a price at all. The charge appears only when the server engine is switched on.
An optimiser sweep is one charge, not one per run. Many backtests, ranked in one job — which is why it costs
five rather than one each.
A paper fill costs the same as nothing much — five hundredths of a credit — but it is per fill, so a high-frequency
paper strategy is the one case where the smallest meter in the product adds up.
A paper deploy pays the same daily rate as a live one. Same engine, same infrastructure.
An empty balance never touches an open position. Running out of credits blocks new algo entries only. Exits, stop-losses and
open positions are explicitly never affected by a billing state — the product refuses to let a billing problem become a market problem
(§17).
178
[PAGE 178 END]
10 Portfolio, quant and deal work A N A LY T I C S  P R I C E S  ·  1 0
All fixed prices, all for a server-side computation. Every equivalent model that runs locally is free, which covers most of
what these tabs do.
