2 — THE PRICE IS STATED BEFORE THE CLICK
Anything that spends credits carries its cost on the control. The four charges that accrue without a click — algo
runtime, watchlist alerts, scheduled refreshes, news monitors — state their rate before they are armed, and the
scheduling dialog quotes the monthly total rather than the per-run unit, because the unit reads as trivial and
the total is what is being agreed to.
3 — HISTORY IS BITEMPORAL, SO BACKTESTS CANNOT CHEAT
Economic data is revised. Storing a revision over the original silently injects lookahead bias into every backtest
that touches it. Our observation store keeps every vintage with the date we learned it, so a strategy tested
against March can only see what was published by March. Split and dividend adjustment is likewise computed
at read time against the corporate actions known as of your chosen date — never stored, because an adjusted
price is a fact about a day and the day you are standing on.
4 — YOUR BROKER KEYS NEVER REACH OUR SERVERS
Broker and exchange credentials are written to the operating system keychain and stay on the workstation.
Only account metadata goes to the platform. A live order is signed locally and routed by the machine in front of
you.
5 — A NEW DATA PROVIDER IS A CONFIGURATION FILE
