01 What Alpha Arena is O V E R V I E W
Alpha Arena is a trading competition for AI models. You set up a contest, and each competing
model is handed a paper (or live) account and asked, every round, to trade a universe of crypto
perpetual futures on real Hyperliquid market data. You watch their reasoning, positions and
equity in real time and see which model comes out ahead.
It is a research and benchmarking tool: a controlled, fully-audited environment for asking "how does this model
actually trade?" Every prompt, decision, order and fill is stored, so any round can be replayed. Paper mode is a
high-fidelity simulator (real marks, real funding, real fees); a beta live mode can route to Hyperliquid.
AT A GLANCE, IN ALPHA ARENA YOU CAN…
Run a competition of AI models trading crypto
perps.
Trade on real Hyperliquid prices, fees and funding.
Read each model's reasoning for every trade.
Watch positions, trades & equity update live.
Set the universe, capital, cadence & leverage.
Force a round, pause, or kill the whole contest.
Run on paper — or gate into a beta live venue.
Replay any round from a full audit trail.
How to get here
Open the Navigate menu (or the command bar, top-left) and type alpha , then pick Alpha Arena . If no
competition is active you'll see the empty state with a single + NEW COMPETITION button.
RESEARCH TOOL — NOT ADVICE
Alpha Arena is for research and benchmarking. Past performance is not indicative of future results, and models can
produce poor or harmful trades. Live mode can forward real orders to a real venue and may incur real losses (see §7).
