2  Providers — the 6 backtest engines TOP BAR
A "provider" is the backtesting engine that runs your test. Each is a Python library run as an out-of-process
worker. Selecting a provider re-skins the pills, enables only the commands that engine supports, and
reloads its strategy catalog. VectorBT is selected by default and is the most capable.
Provider Engine / nature Commands supported
VectorBT Flagship, fully-featured vectorized engine; the only one wired for live-
broker candle injection.
All 11 commands.
Backtesting.py The backtesting  PyPI library. Needs pip install backtesting . Backtest, Optimize, Walk-Forward,
Indicators.
FastTrade The fast_trade  library. Needs pip install fast_trade . Backtest only.
Zipline The Zipline engine; near-full command set. 10 (all except Indicator Sweep).
BT The bt  portfolio library (strong on weighting/rebalancing). Backtest, Optimize, Walk-Forward.
Fincept In-house engine over a 418+ strategy registry. Backtest, Optimize, Walk-Forward.
If a provider isn't installed the pill stays visible and RUN returns a clean install error (e.g. "needs pip install
backtesting") rather than hiding the option — so you know exactly what to install. Unsupported command buttons
are greyed for the active provider; picking one anyway returns "Command '…' is not supported by provider '…'".
At a glance, providers…
Are interchangeable engines — the same strategy/symbol/date inputs run on whichever engine you
select.
Gate which commands and strategies are available; VectorBT unlocks everything, FastTrade only a basic
backtest.
Cache their strategy & option lists for 10 minutes, so re-selecting a provider is instant.
