05 How credits work T H E  M E T E R  ·  0 5
Credits meter consumption — the things that cost us money when you use them, which in
practice means AI inference and a small number of expensive computations. They do not gate
access to anything.
WHAT A CREDIT IS
Roughly a thousand tokens of language-model work. Every action costs between one and twenty-five credits,
except the one that is deliberately smaller: a filled paper trade costs 0.05, twenty fills to the credit, because a
simulator people hesitate to use is a broken simulator.
WHAT IS FREE, PERMANENTLY
N O  C R E D I T  I S  E V E R  C H A R G E D  F O R  A N Y  O F  T H E S E
Every quote, chart, order book, tape and layout. Reading the tape is the product.
Placing, modifying and cancelling orders — paper or live. Live orders route through your own broker keys,
so they cost us nothing and are free forever.
Loading and charting any data series, within a generous monthly allowance of distinct series, and re-
loading anything you already opened this month.
Every local analytic model — derivatives, M&A, alternatives, technicals. They run on your machine in C++,
so there is nothing to bill.
Notebooks, spreadsheet, notes, reports, dashboards, watchlists, the node editor and every screen in
the terminal.
Typing. Voice is metered per minute because a vendor bills us per minute; the keyboard is not.
THE FOUR RULES THE METER FOLLOWS
Rule What it means for you
The price is on the control Every metered button states its cost before you press it. Nothing is discovered on the
invoice.
Charged before the work,
refunded on failure
If our provider fails, our sidecar times out or you cancel, the reservation is released. Our
outage is not your bill.
Only the server can
charge
There is no endpoint a client can call to declare a spend. The ledger is not under the
application's control, or yours.
Running out never breaks
a position
An algorithm that cannot pay its runtime stops opening and keeps every exit, stop and
bracket armed. Alerts stay armed too.
FINCEPT TERMINAL  ·  05 PLANS & PRICING 9
76
[PAGE 76 END]
06 The price list T H E  M E T E R  ·  0 6
The complete meter. Flat prices cost exactly what is listed; measured prices are the typical total
for a normal run, and you are charged the actual usage.
